    "Introduce an embodied local feedback mechanism in the material itself, for example engineering bacteria to sense matrix degradation products, local stiffness, or light-generated fragments and respond by expressing or activating crosslinkers, degradation enzymes, or motility regulators, so control is distributed biologically rather than only computed externally.",
    "Make the metabolite-responsive phase-separated organelle mechanistically write into the matrix by sequestering or releasing a protease, crosslinker, photosensitizer, or degradation inhibitor, thereby coupling intracellular metabolic state directly to extracellular photodegradability in a new way.",
    "Develop a distinct state/control variable not present in the references, such as a quantifiable tension-sensitive or cleavage-sensitive PenTag anchor state that is optically readable and actively tunable, enabling a mechanochemical closed loop rather than a standard light-dose model-predictive control loop."
