        {
          "inspiration": "An Efficient Platform and Communication Architecture for Event-triggered Cyber-physical Systems",
          "concept": "Threshold-based event-triggered actuation that updates the system only when sensed states cross meaningful thresholds, reducing unnecessary actuation and preserving resources.",
          "adaptation": "The phase-separated synthetic organelle converts ligand release from cleaved PenTag anchors into a biochemical event trigger: repair effector expression is activated only when local damage ligand concentration exceeds a threshold, rather than being continuously expressed or externally scheduled.",
          "citation": "[Author et al., 2018](https://openalex.org/W2808897733)"
